    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d337">

                <pb facs="0371" n="281" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/10704</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-07-13T17:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 13, 1918,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 14, 2.55 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am reliably informed that the General Staff is urging upon the Cabinet the
                    immediate occupation of Manchuria by Japanese troops as this can be done now
                    without offense to China because of the recent military agreement.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d337-f1"/> The plan submitted includes taking over the control of
                    the Chinese Eastern Railway. The Cabinet met yesterday to consider this proposal
                    which if approved will be submitted to the Advisory Council which is to meet
                    to-day.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
